    schema:description "About us Distribusion is the world’s leading ground transportation marketplace and gives travellers seamless access to ground transportation online, from search to ticket purchase. We have built a cutting-edge B2B technology platform that connects bus, rail, and ferry operators in 70+ countries with the biggest online retailers, including Google Maps and Booking.com. We are shaping the future of travel and building the largest global network of transport providers and retailers. We are one of the fastest-growing startups in travel, backed by leading venture capital investors including TQ Ventures, Lightrock, Creandum, and Northzone, and are headquartered in Berlin, Germany. Following our recent $80m Series C funding, we are ready to push beyond. The opportunity We are looking for a Director of Global Integrations Delivery, whom we prefer to describe internally as Supply, to lead and execute our global integration strategies and deliver outstanding solutions to key stakeholders across multiple markets. This role manages six teams globally and reports directly to the CEO. What you’ll do Lead Integrations Strategy: Take ownership of the strategic direction and roadmap for the Integrations team, ensuring alignment with overall business goals and driving automation and innovation within integrations. Product and Project Leadership: Oversee the scoping, execution, and delivery of technical integration projects, including onboarding new carriers, and creating data-driven solutions that add value to our stakeholders. Cross-Functional Collaboration: Work closely with engineering, product, operations, and business teams to ensure seamless integrations, drive process improvements, and facilitate effective communication across teams. Stakeholder Management: Build and maintain strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders, including C-level executives, to drive integration initiatives forward. Process Optimisation: Identify opportunities for process improvements across product management, Jira usage, reporting systems, and overall delivery, helping the team to scale effectively. Leadership and Mentoring: Lead and mentor a diverse team of integration experts, product managers, and engineers, fostering a culture of continuous learning and excellence. Global Expansion: Own the delivery of integration projects and carrier onboarding strategies in new regions (Europe, LATAM, SEA) to ensure scalability and drive business growth. Workplace: Berlin & Hybrid We are mainly looking for this role to be based in Germany, preferably in our headquarters in Berlin. Who You Are Experience: 5+ years of experience in technical product management, project management, operations management or integrations management, with hands-on experience in leading complex integrations in API and data product environments. Leadership: Proven leadership experience with a track record of managing technical teams to deliver results on time and within scope. Stakeholder Influence: Strong ability to build relationships and influence stakeholders at all levels, including C-level executives, with a focus on collaboration and driving strategic decision-making. Technical Expertise: Experience working with large-scale products and systems. Process-Oriented: Experience implementing process improvements in project management tools (e.g., Jira), reporting systems, and delivery methodologies to ensure consistent, high-quality results. Global Perspective: Comfortable managing international teams and integration strategies across diverse regions (Europe, LATAM, SEA). Education: A degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field. A technical background is essential to effectively engage with the development team and stakeholders. Languages: Fluent in English (both verbal and written). Knowledge of additional languages (e.g., Spanish) is a plus. What you can expect: Make a global impact. Help shape how millions of people discover and book ground transportation worldwide. Own your work. Take responsibility from day one and see the direct impact of your contributions. Build with the best tools. We move fast, continuously evolve our tech stack, and invest in modern, efficient solutions. Work with industry leaders. Our partners include Booking.com, Google Maps, Amtrak, Deutsche Bahn, Renfe, and SNCF. Grow with exceptional people. Join an international team that will challenge, support, and inspire you every day. Work your way. Enjoy flexible and remote-friendly working options, relocation opportunities, and plenty of room to grow. Our hiring team for this role: For any queries, please contact Ana Valentim, your Talent Partner at (). Do you want to work on a product that is used by millions of people daily with a high load, availability, scalability and the most advanced technology? Come join us! Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
