    schema:description "<p><strong>Job title: </strong>Director of Product &amp; Tech Delivery<br><strong>Location:</strong> Bristol or London (hybrid)<em><br></em><strong>Salary:</strong> £130,400 - £163,000<br><strong>Team:</strong> Product &amp; Tech Operations<br><strong>Reporting to:</strong> VP Product &amp; Tech Operations</p> <p><em>This role is based in either Bristol or London and requires an existing right to work in the UK.</em></p> <p><em>At this time, we are not able to offer visa sponsorship for this role. We are committed to building a diverse, global team and our sponsorship policy is evaluated on a role-by-role basis. We encourage you to keep an eye on our careers site to stay informed about future opportunities where we are able to offer visa sponsorship.</em></p> <p>Kaluza is the Energy Intelligence Platform, turning energy complexity into seamless coordination. We help energy companies overcome today's challenges while accelerating the shift to a clean, electrified future. Leveraging Data, AI, and real-time decision-making we turn energy complexity into growth opportunities for our partners.&nbsp;</p> <p>By combining predictive algorithms with human-centred design, Kaluza makes clean energy dependable and affordable.</p> <p>With teams across Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, and a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corporation in Japan, we power leading companies including OVO, AGL and ENGIE, as well as innovators like Volvo and Volkswagen</p> <p><strong>What will I be doing?</strong></p> <p>Reporting to the VP Product &amp; Tech Operations, you’ll own the timely, predictable execution of our Product &amp; Technology roadmap, for Kaluza and for our clients, across our global product, field deployment, and platform foundations teams. You’ll line-manage Heads and Group Delivery Managers, set the standard for how delivery is done across the function, and provide the leadership confidence around what we can deliver, both near-term and further ahead. You’ll move fluently between board-level narrative and the detail of a single stuck dependency.</p> <p><strong>The role spans four focus areas:</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Run delivery at scale </strong>- own predictable, end-to-end execution across your portfolio.</li> <li><strong>Implementing an AI-native system of wor</strong>k - make AI-assisted delivery the default and raise the bar on how delivery is done, partnering with our P&amp;T business operations team to implement best practices across our product development lifecycle (PDLC) that are designed and standardised by the Business Operations team.</li> <li><strong>Grow an independent, high-performing delivery community</strong> - build a function that solves its own problems, and has a “yes if” attitude to solving the inevitable challenges of the day to day.</li> <li><strong>Partner and Influence at the Executive Level&nbsp;</strong></li> </ul> <h1><span style=\"font-size: 18pt;\"><strong>Run delivery at scale</strong></span></h1> <p>Own and drive successful delivery across Kaluza’s Product and Tech organisation, typically multiple streams that may align to client programmes or global initiatives.</p> <ul> <li>Own end-to-end delivery of the Product &amp; Tech roadmap across your area, e.g. across multiple client streams (OVO &amp; ENGIE in Europe, AGL &amp; Shell in APAC) or multiple global product streams.</li> <li>Implement evolutions of a standard methodology that allows the business to scale and ensures successful client implementations</li> <li>Drive absolute roadmap alignment, delivery enablement and reporting at multiple levels, from team detail to executive overview.</li> <li>Bring confidence to what we can deliver, near-term and further ahead through robust capacity planning, milestone tracking (actuals vs estimates), forecasting, and proactive management and resolution of cross-team dependencies.</li> <li>Partner with Product, Engineering, UX and Client Delivery leadership so deliverables meet client capabilities, support needs and timelines, and so client feedback flows back into the delivery process.</li> <li>Provide objective, data-led neutral insight on how delivery is really going; proactively escalate risks and issues early, and drive decisions with senior leadership and clients.</li> <li>Embed good practices into our internal delivery management practices that are developed by the Business Operations team, and provide input to shape their future roadmap.&nbsp;</li> <li>Deputise for the VP when needed.</li> </ul> <h1><span style=\"font-size: 18pt;\"><strong>Implement an AI-native system of work through delivery</strong></span></h1> <p>Lead the strategic evolution of our delivery practices by embedding AI-assisted methodologies into default operational workflows</p> <ul> <li>Embed AI-assisted delivery into reporting, forecasting, capacity and effort analysis, dependency mapping, risk detection and status communication.</li> <li>Push the boundaries of Jira, JQL and agentic workflows; build dashboards and reporting that drive development forward at pace and replace manual effort.</li> <li>Simplify and standardise practice across Product &amp; Tech: refine ways of working, embed Agile &amp; Lean practice, and raise predictability and the effort-to-value ratio in your area.</li> <li>Act as a change driver, co-own the delivery of a roadmap of improvements to our system of work alongside Business Operations, and bring people with you through the change.</li> <li>Champion continuous improvement and show the function what good, AI-native delivery looks like in practice.</li> </ul> <h1><span style=\"font-size: 18pt;\"><strong>Grow an independent, high-performing delivery community</strong></span></h1> <p>Build a self-sufficient, empowered function that is a gold standard for getting things done, effectively, and with transparency.</p> <ul> <li>Lead and develop a group of people leaders and delivery managers, Heads of, Group and Lead) Delivery Managers, setting clear objectives, focus and clarity.</li> <li>Coach the team to navigate complexity and uncertainty, to self-solve, and to bias their effort towards Kaluza’s goals and our client commitments.</li> <li>Know the product and coach the team to understand the product domain for their area so that they can enable cross-functional team delivery of the product roadmap and client delivery goals</li> <li>Mentor and upskill across the community; show the team what good looks like and raise the standard across the board.</li> <li>Clear the barriers that stop Product teams focusing on innovation and strategy, and Engineering teams focusing on technical excellence and execution.</li> <li>Support the Delivery function in achieving its strategy and goals, and champion the wider change and planning agenda.</li> <li>Be an innovative thinker and member of the larger Kaluza SLT team to drive the business forward.</li> </ul> <h1><span style=\"font-size: 18pt;\"><strong>Partner and Influence at the Executive Level&nbsp;</strong></span></h1> <ul> <li>Act as a trusted partner to Product, Engineering, UX, and Client Delivery leadership, serving as an active member of the Senior Leadership Team (SLT)&nbsp;</li> <li>Confidently manage relationships with C-level clients.&nbsp;</li> <li>Deliver objective tracking, milestone visibility + forecasting, and proactive risk mitigation strategies to leadership, while serving as a strategic deputy for the VP of Product &amp; Tech Operations when required</li> </ul> <p><strong>About You</strong></p> <p>You’re an accomplished delivery leader with a strong track record. Ideally, you’ll be:</p> <ul> <li>A builder <em>and</em> an executor: you define what good looks like, take full accountability, and go looking for what you need rather than waiting for a brief.</li> <li>Genuinely AI-native: AI tools feel like leverage, not an afterthought. You have deep curiosity in innovation and AI tools, actively pushing AI adoption into delivery practice.</li> <li>Steady in ambiguity: A nimble leader who thrives in complex undefined spaces, is comfortable diving into problems at multiple altitudes, and the steady presence others rely on when the path isn’t fully defined.</li> <li>Strategic Delivery Leader: An accomplished delivery leader and a bar raiser when it comes to of managing large-scale, cross-functional delivery management functions within a high-growth SaaS environment</li> <li>Experienced leading delivery management at scale: line-managing and developing people leaders, across cross-functional Product &amp; Engineering teams using agile methodologies.</li> <li>Able to design and evolve delivery operating models, governance and ways of working, with an openness to follow current Kaluza practice and refine where needed.</li> <li>A trusted partner: to Product &amp; Engineering leadership, able to influence senior leadership,and credible with C-level clients.</li> <li>A strong listener, people leader <em>and</em> coach: able to empower teams and colleagues to reach their full potential, and to bring people along on a change journey.</li> <li>Fluent with Jira, or similar roadmapping tools, with real curiosity about using JQL and AI to generate dashboards and reporting that drive development at pace.</li> <li>Comfortable switching between team-level detail and executive-level overview, applying the right approach in the right context.</li> <li>Committed to radical candour: you ask hard questions, and give honest developmental feedback.</li> </ul> <p><strong>What will set you apart</strong></p> <ul> <li>Extensive experience managing delivery frameworks across major global energy utility accounts or multi-regional client programmes.</li> <li>A proven background or curiosity in implementing an AI-integrated Product Development Lifecycle alongside business operations teams.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Where you'll work</strong></p> <p>We offer flexible working, with a requirement of 3 days a week in the office. This gives us the best of both: real time together to collaborate and build relationships, with the flexibility to work in the way that suits you best the rest of the week.</p> <p><strong>Kaluza Values</strong></p> <p>Here at Kaluza we have five core values that guide us as a business:</p> <p><strong><em>Play to win, Solve the real problem, Build trust every day, Own the outcome, Go further together.</em></strong></p> <p><strong>Our Perks</strong></p> <ul> <li>Pension Scheme</li> <li>Discretionary Bonus Scheme</li> <li>Private Medical Insurance + Virtual GP</li> <li>Life Assurance</li> <li>Access to Furthr - a Climate Action app</li> <li>Free Mortgage Advice and Eye Tests</li> <li>Perks at Work - access to thousands of retail discounts</li> <li>5% Flex Fund - to spend on the benefits you want most</li> <li>26 days holiday + bank holidays</li> <li>Progressive Leave Policy - With no qualifying service periods, including up to 26 weeks full pay for primary caregivers and 4 weeks full pay for secondary caregivers when welcoming a new addition to your family.</li> <li>Personal Learning Budget - Upskill, learn and grow!</li> <li>Home Office Budget</li> <li>And more!</li> </ul> <p><strong>We want the best people</strong></p> <p>We’re keen to meet people from all walks of life. Our view is that the more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We want to build teams which represent a variety of experiences, perspectives and skills, and we recognise talent on the basis of merit and potential.</p> <p>We understand some people may not apply for jobs unless they tick every box. But if you're excited about joining us and think you have some of what we're looking for, even if you're not 100% sure, we'd still love to hear from you.</p> <p>Find out more about working in <a href=\"http://kaluza.com\">Kaluza</a> on our <a href=\"https://kaluza-dev.webflow.io/careers\">careers page</a> and <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaluza/\">LinkedIn</a>. <br><br>You can also find our Applicant Data Protection Policy <a href=\"https://www.kaluza.com/applicant-data-protection-notice\">here</a>.</p> <p><br><br><br></p> Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-kaluza ;
