<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-junior-clinical-fellow-winnersh-280711> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-21T10:34:54+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/montu-uk/junior-clinical-fellow-winnersh-280711> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "848a53735a8fbd022211e8a89b8e90c60e967872b0d4020156b83db05c1b533d" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-21T08:46:28+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-21T10:34:54+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "junior-clinical-fellow-winnersh-280711" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-21"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Be at the forefront of a new era in patient care Are you a doctor who has completed Foundation Training and is looking for a unique clinical opportunity? This is your chance to work at the cutting edge of cannabis based medicines, supporting patients with complex and often life changing conditions while gaining experience in an emerging area of medicine. Join a passionate and forward thinking clinical team in a rapidly growing field where no two patients, or days, are the same. You will work alongside experienced consultants, pharmacists and multidisciplinary specialists, contributing to meaningful patient outcomes while developing your clinical expertise in a progressive and innovative healthcare environment. This role is offered as a 12 month fixed term contract What is the job? We are recruiting a Junior Clinical Fellow to join our London team. This is a hands-on, patient focused role where you will play a critical part in prescribing and reviewing cannabis-based medicines for patients with complex clinical needs. Your work will centre on delivering safe, effective and highly personalised treatment, supporting patients across a wide range of conditions. Collaboration is at the heart of what we do. You will work closely with a multidisciplinary clinical team, contributing not only to outstanding patient outcomes but also to the development of clinical pathways, education initiatives, and service improvements. This role offers a genuine opportunity to grow your expertise and make a lasting impact in a fast-evolving specialty. This is a full time role contracted at 40 hours per week. Your time will be split across three days on site and two days working remotely, with one Saturday per month required on site. Saturday working is compensated with a day in lieu. What will you be doing? Conduct clinical reviews via video call with patients during their journey through the clinic. Prescribe medicines and tailor treatments to individual patient needs. Provide expert guidance to patients on treatment options. Clinically check and review CBPM prescriptions for safety and accuracy. Help to answer complex clinical queries and provide guidance to our patient support and other external teams. Maintain accurate patient records in line with GMC standards. Deliver education and training on CBPM to patients, clinicians, and staff. Collaborate with the wider team to streamline processes and improve outcomes. What do you need? Registered medical practitioner with the GMC and a full licence to practice Completion of Foundation Year 2 (F2) training or equivalent clinical experience including a placement in GP or A&E. Experience working in a clinical setting Knowledge of CBPM is desired not essential or willingness to undergo specialised training Clear and confident communicator across clinical and non-clinical settings Highly effective at managing time and prioritising competing demands Proactive and resourceful when identifying and resolving problems Well-organised, detail-oriented, and able to manage complex workflows What we offer: Generous Leave: 25 days holiday (rising to 27 after year one and 30 after year three) + 8 bank holidays Pension Matching: Up to 5% employer matching contributions Flexibility and Wellness: Work-from-home options, cycle-to-work scheme, and more Growth Opportunities: Collaborate across teams and represent Montu at events, with support to grow your skills and impact Enhanced Maternity & Paternity Leave About Us Montu UK is a leading digital health company specialising in cannabis-based medicines (CBPM), dedicated to improving patient access to safe and effective treatments. Our mission is to transform lives by combining innovative technology with high-quality clinical care, ensuring patients receive the support they need at every step of their journey. As a fast-growing organisation, we offer a collaborative and supportive environment where talented people can develop their careers while contributing to meaningful change in healthcare. At Montu UK, your work has a direct impact on improving patients’ lives and expanding access to modern medical treatments. Compensation: £60K • £60K Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
