    schema:description "At DemoUp Cliplister, we’re not just about content creation; we’re revolutionizing how over 3,000 brands and retailers like MediaMarkt, Otto, Fnac, Microsoft, Logitech, and Bosch bring their products to life with innovative solutions like video, augmented reality, and user-generated content. Our unique approach combines content creation services with a state-of-the-art digital asset management platform and content syndication, making us a key SaaS player in Europe’s retail landscape. Join us to expand our network and make an impact! Your role and your tasks: As our Senior Product Manager (m/f/x), you will own the end-to-end management of our content syndication product lifecycle — our highest-revenue product lines — in close collaboration with our sales, engineering, and customer support teams. You will: Own the product vision: shape how brands present and optimize their product pages, building on our strength in video syndication. Expand our syndication capabilities: help us grow beyond video into richer product content — images, enhanced content, and detailed product information. Build compliance into the workflow: ensure product data is trustworthy and compliant with evolving e-commerce regulations. Think business-first, not features-first: define and own the KPIs that matter, and understand the revenue and sales impact of your work. Own the roadmap: prioritize initiatives based on customer needs, market trends, and business goals, working closely with sales, engineering, and customer support. Now let's talk about you: 5+ years in product management in the SaaS space, digital content, e-commerce, or related fields. A proven, numbers-driven track record — you know your data and can speak to your impact. Strong AI knowledge with a hands-on project to show. Business fluency in German and English. Senior presence, confidence, and a hands-on, cooperative mindset. The perks of working with us: Build and expand your network in our exciting customer portfolio with global brands like Philips, Samsung, Bosch, Adidas, and many more. Opportunity to work on innovative products that make a difference in the digital content landscape. Report directly to the Chief Product Officer - quick decision making and flat hierarchy. Flexible working options, 30 vacation days plus 30 days remote working within the EU/year. Enjoy perks like corporate benefits, Urban Sports and Deutschland ticket subsidies. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
