    schema:description "We’re on the lookout for an ambitious Senior Product Designer to join our Design Team at our office in Berlin. Join us in building the largest AI enabled fintech for healthcare! About Nelly We are building the AI-Driven Financial Operating System for European healthcare, solving the biggest challenges for patients and practices. We create what no bank or software platform can handle. Our all-in-one platform transforms chaotic administrative processes into intelligent, automated workflows, from patient care to billing to next-generation payments. Because we truly believe: healthcare should be less about paperwork and more about people. Why? Because Europe is facing a massive shortage of medical professionals. And if we don't rethink the way practices work, the system won't be able to keep up. With our Series B funding of over €50 million from world-class investors, we are turning our vision into reality. What sets us apart: We work with the best team, which is why we give everything together every day. We believe in Talent Density, because exceptional people make everyone around them better. At Nelly, we move fast and expect everyone to keep up. Stagnation isn’t an option, which is why we invest heavily in growth. AI isn't a nice-to-have at Nelly. We expect you to use it every day and give you everything you need to do so. You get trust and ownership and we expect you to speak up, even when it's uncomfortable. Joining us, you will: Own end-to-end UX for a specific product area once team/pod assignments are finalized — from discovery through shipped feature Contribute meaningfully to evolving Nelly's design system/design language for consistency across the product Help move core product metrics (conversion, task completion) through better UX in owned flows Support the design team's process and structure as it scales What you'll bring: End-to-end product design craft: UX flows, interaction design, and polished UI, from discovery through implementation Comfortable owning ambiguity and driving decisions with limited guidance in a fast-moving startup environment Strong collaboration with PMs and engineers — can work directly from problem statement to shipped feature Contributes to and helps evolve a design system/design language, not just uses one Experience Scope (Seniority): 3+ years in product design roles, including some in a scale-up/high-growth environment Comfortable in a small team with high individual ownership (little hand-holding, few layers of review) Our Interview Process: First call with TA Second online call with Head of Design Case Study and meet the team What we offer: Deutschlandticket (public transport pass covering all of Germany) or Swapfiets membership, so you get around the city fast Urban Sports Club membership, for sport and balance Flexible working hours and a hybrid setup Up to 4 weeks of workation 500€ L&D Budget A dog-friendly office with great vibes and a team that's fun to work with Snacks and a fridge full of cold drinks We welcome applications from people of all genders and backgrounds, regardless of origin or age. If you're convinced you're the right fit for this role - even if your CV doesn't match the requirements 100% - tell us why. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
