    schema:datePosted "2026-08-21"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "WunderGraph is a fast-growing startup, our goal is to bring everybody together to build digital products end-to-end. From interface design to API implementation, we provide the platform to go from sketch to product in a category-defining collaborative experience. Our North Star is to take the friction out of bringing digital ideas to life, making room for your ideas and productivity. Developers from some of the biggest companies in the world are using WunderGraph to design and streamline their API environments. We raised our Series A ($7.5 million USD) in March 2025, being backed by eBay, Karma Ventures, and Aspenwood Ventures. The culture we are creating together is extremely important to us. Read here how we are Building the Company We Always Wanted to Work In. We invite everyone that wants to join us to understand our Core Beliefs and if you want to make an impact, have your voice heard, and work in a no-BS organization where you can get stuff done, look no further and apply today so we can chat. ABOUT THE ROLE As a Senior Product Designer at WunderGraph, you are the connection between what our users will find most helpful and what our engineers build. Considering the users also happen to be other developers, this becomes an interesting challenge to think about the Developer Experience as the User Experience. You combine sharp user insight, craft, and pragmatism to deliver experiences that are elegant, usable, and built to scale. This is a wide-reaching role, as design roles at a startup should be. One week you might be running user interviews to shape a new feature; the next, refining our design system or designing a marketing landing page. You ground your work in evidence rather than assumption, partner closely with product and engineering, and turn what you learn about users into a clear, informed UX strategy that guides where we go next. TEAM INTEGRATION Reports to the VP of Product; is part of the Product team Aligns closely with the CEO (Product) and Head of Customer Success (customer experience and business impact) Collaborate within the Product team with the Delivery Lead and the Design Engineer Collaborates cross-functionally with engineering, marketing, product, and customer success ROLE OBJECTIVES You are successful if you: Take ownership of the complete design lifecycle, bridging the gap between initial discovery and final delivery for web and product interfaces. Cultivate an evidence-based UX strategy that leverages user research and data to steer the product's evolution. Oversee the growth of a unified and extensible design system that spans both our product and marketing efforts. Convert user insights and organizational objectives into pragmatic, human-centric solutions engineered for long-term scalability. Advocate for excellence in accessibility, responsiveness, and performance as fundamental pillars of your craft. Provide mentorship to the team, sharing expertise in research methodologies and design principles. Refine the visual and functional identity of WunderGraph through meticulous and high-impact design work. Impact high-level product strategy by demonstrating how user-focused decisions drive tangible business impact. ROLE TASKS The role focuses on, but is not limited to: Product Design Design and prototype user flows, interfaces, and interactions with scalability in mind. Own design problems end to end. From initial concept through execution and iteration after launch. Rapidly produce wireframes, prototypes, and high-fidelity designs, exploring multiple concepts and iterating quickly. Define and evolve our design system and component library, keeping it consistent and maintainable. Partner closely with engineers on feasibility, quality, and handoff, contributing to technical decisions (and coding where you're comfortable and it helps as a plus, not a requirement). Introduce advanced prototyping, interaction design, and motion practices. UX Research & Strategy Plan and conduct user research across discovery and validation via user interviews, surveys, usability testing, and competitor analysis. Turn ambiguous product questions into decision-grade research that maps to real product and design decisions. Synthesize findings into clear insights, personas, journey maps, and opportunity areas that the team can act on. Build and maintain a shared insight repository so learning is reusable, searchable, and available to everyone. Translate research into an informed, evolving UX strategy that guides the roadmap and anchors design direction in real user needs. Advocate for the user in prioritization and roadmap discussions, and define what \"better\" looks like through clear UX success metrics. Run discovery workshops and share insights so research shows up where decisions are made like in design reviews, product planning, and standups embedding user knowledge from the get-go. Web & Brand Experience Own the design and evolution of WunderGraph's web presence. Deliver assets that span product and marketing: landing pages, visuals, campaign graphics, and interactive components. Shape and maintain a cohesive style guide, balancing design innovation with consistency. Support brand storytelling with motion graphics and interactive elements. ROLE REQUIREMENTS Senior-level experience in Product Design or UX/UI Design, with a strong portfolio of shipped work. Proven experience planning and running UX research (both generative and evaluative) and turning findings into strategy. Proficiency in Figma, prototyping tools, and Adobe Creative Suite. Strong background in UX and interaction design, accessibility, responsive design, and usability. Experience contributing to or leading design systems and component libraries. Comfortable using data and research to inform and defend design decisions. Working knowledge of front-end technologies (HTML/CSS, JavaScript a plus) enough to collaborate closely with engineers. Excellent communication, storytelling, and collaboration skills in English. A self-starter who is comfortable with ambiguity and can lead initiatives independently in a fast-moving startup. Comfortable working 100% remotely in a distributed team. Willingness to travel occasionally for team retreats and workshops. Why WunderGraph? Work from wherever you thrive—we’re fully remote and globally distributed. If you're in Miami, come work with us in person! We also provide co-working space options worldwide if needed. Pick your preferred work hardware We focus on getting stuff done, and on having fun whilst doing so: work hard, play hard! You can make a real difference and find lots of opportunities to grow together with us Discretionary PTO: take the time you need to recharge Competitive compensation Depending on location, we offer healthcare benefits according to local standards Team retreats across the globe Note: This is a full-time, fully remote position. We are looking for someone who is available to work during European (CET) business hours. The Process We respect your time and interest in WunderGraph. This is why we're aiming to make the process as fast as possible. Here's what you can expect: 30 min intro call with Mariya from our People team 45 min discussion with the hiring manager. Following this, you might receive a small take home assignment related to the role. This is your chance to prove your skill! Complete the assignment and review together with hiring manager Meet the founders Culture fit call with team members Offer Our process also includes reference and background checks. We aim to respond or provide feedback in 2 or 3 days between each stage of the process. We're usually hiring through Deel as our Employer of Record, except for Germany or Florida where we're hiring directly. WunderGraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds. You can find out more about our ways of working together here: WunderGraph Public Handbook and Resources We’re looking forward to your application so we can grow together! Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
