<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-staff-product-designer-london-408714> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-21T10:34:54+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/legora/staff-product-designer-london-408714> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "b128d8ffc92218b4b41a915cdf849465d0c5ab25bf641266a5da7e528b65c6f2" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-20T18:46:07+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-21T10:34:54+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "staff-product-designer-london-408714" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About Us Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar. Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes. 1,000+ customers across 50+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White & Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to $100M+ in ARR, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI and Graceview. We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law. Joining Legora means three things. We lean in: ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions. We fight for excellence: high standards, direct, ego-free feedback. We grow together: as a team and with our customers. Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts. If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place. As a Staff Product Designer, you’ll be the first designer in our London office, taking on some of our most complex product challenges and setting a high bar for design quality across products and teams. You’ll partner closely with product and engineering to shape direction, bring clarity to ambiguous problems, and deliver best-in-class interaction and visual design. This is a highly hands-on role for a designer who can move between product strategy and craft, and whose work raises the quality of the team around them. What you’ll do Lead design across multiple product areas, creating coherence across complex workflows and experiences. Shape product strategy: frame the hardest problems, influence roadmaps, and turn ambiguity into bold, practical solutions. Set and raise the bar for design craft, accessibility, and usability across Legora’s product. Partner with product and engineering to make smart tradeoffs that protect the experience while shipping quickly. Explore new product directions, from zero-to-one concepts to scaled launches. Explore and implement new ways of working with AI to produce better design outcomes, faster. Help make Legora a destination for exceptional design talent in London. About you Extensive product design experience with a track record of shipping complex, high-impact products. Exceptional craft in interaction and visual design, with the ability to connect the details to the bigger picture. Comfortable owning complex, ambiguous problems and creating clarity across teams and product areas. Skilled at moving seamlessly between hands-on design and product strategy. Strong product judgment and communication skills; you influence direction and inspire confidence across product, engineering, and leadership. What’s in it for you Career development opportunities in a rapidly evolving entrepreneurial environment. Direct collaboration with senior leadership and the opportunity to impact company growth and strategy. A collaborative, high-energy team where your ideas and contributions are valued and implemented. Competitive salary complemented by a transparent and highly competitive options program. Legora is an Equal Opportunity Employer At Legora, we believe great teams are built on diversity of thought and experience. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive, high-performance culture where everyone can do their best work. We welcome people of all backgrounds and don’t discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
