    schema:description "Are you looking to start your career in pharmacy and gain valuable experience in a supportive and innovative environment? Join our dedicated team in Winnersh, where you will play a vital role in supporting pharmacy operations behind the scenes. As a Trainee Pharmacy Dispenser, you will work closely with an experienced team to develop your skills and knowledge while contributing to safe and efficient patient care. The Role: As a Trainee Pharmacy Dispenser, you will be supported and trained to carry out duties such as: Learning how to dispense medication accurately while ensuring compliance with legal and regulatory standards Supporting the Pharmacy Operations Team with stock control, inventory management, and dispensing processes Assisting in the delivery of exceptional service to patients and healthcare professionals Developing the skills to maintain accurate records and contribute to the smooth running of the pharmacy What we are looking for: A genuine interest in pharmacy and a desire to become a qualified dispenser Strong attention to detail and a willingness to learn Good communication skills and the ability to work well as part of a team Enthusiasm, motivation, and a proactive approach to developing your skills Ability to work at pace under pressure Flexibility to allow you to grow with a growing organisation What we offer: Salary £25,500 per annum Paid Training so you will be a fully trained Pharmacy dispenser in around 9 months 25 days holiday + bank holidays, increasing to 30 days after 1 year Generous pension scheme with employer contributions matched up to 5% Supportive and welcoming team culture Casual dress Company pension Cycle to work scheme Free food and drink onsite Hours: 40 hours per week Monday to Friday, full-time Shift pattern: 7am to 4pm or 10am to 7pm on a rota basis On-site position Our offices are conveniently located in Winnersh Triangle, with easy transport links and parking available on site. About Montu UK At Montu UK, we are committed to transforming lives through innovative healthcare solutions. As part of our dynamic and friendly team, you will contribute to a mission of delivering excellence in pharmaceutical care, supported by a collaborative environment and opportunities for professional growth. If you are passionate about patient care and want to be part of an innovative, growing company with training opportunities – apply now. Compensation: £12.75 per hour • £26,500 per annum £12.75 per hour Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
